==Battleground==
*20 [[Doge]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
*1 [[Heavenly Hippoe]] spawns after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*5 [[Gabriel]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 10~16.67 seconds<sup>300f~500f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Sunfish Jones]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 10~16.67 seconds<sup>300f~500f</sup>.
**8 [[Gabriel]]s spawn, delay 16.67~23.33 seconds<sup>500f~700f</sup>.
**3 [[Heavenly Hippoe]] spawn, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.
**1 [[R.Ost]] spawns.

==Strategy==
R.Ost and Sunfish Jones. A deadly combination under the right circumstances. Fortunately, they are all on base hit and the beginning of the battle is very similar to that of [[3rd Round: Dawn (Insane)]]. Stall the Heavenly Hippoe, Doges and Gabriels for as long as possible before hitting the base. You will almost have no money on base hit, as your main source of it is Gabriels, which don't drop a lot to begin with. For R.Ost, you use about the same strategy as a lot of other R.Ost stages, [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]], [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Dragon Cat]], [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]] (non-[[True Form]]), [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]], and maybe even [[Bath Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Luxury Bath Cat]] + a whole lot of strong meatshields, most notably [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]] and/or [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Wall Cat]]. Once R.Ost is dead, just chip down Sunfish Jones and win.

